Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 07:28:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 21/22] ttf: without glyph classes, a font that attaches marks
 marks its marks

A font without GDEF glyph classes gets every glyph a base, so that the compiled
font has no glyph classes either and a shaper guesses them as it does for the
binary. But a font with a mark-attachment lookup gets glyph classes from any
compiler, and there every unmarked glyph is a base: Lato's combining accents
(no GDEF, a mark feature) stopped being marks, and 135 of them shaped as bases.
In such a font a glyph whose codepoint is a nonspacing mark, and not
default-ignorable, is now a mark, as HarfBuzz synthesises it (enclosing and
spacing marks, and U+034F, it takes for bases).

Assisted by an AI agent (Claude Opus 5.5)
